{"name":"Whispering Waterfall","hex":"#e3e6db","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whispering","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of whisper"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That whispers.","Associated with whispers. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whispering"},{"term":"waterfall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flow of water over the edge of a cliff.","A waterfall-like outpouring of liquid, smoke, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fall like a waterfall.","To drink (something) from a container by pouring it from a height so as not to touch one's lips to the rim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterfall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whispering","blocks":[{"text":"Whispering is an unvoiced mode of phonation in which the vocal cords are abducted so that they do not vibrate; air passes between the arytenoid cartilages to create audible turbulence during speech. Supralaryngeal articulation remains the same as in normal speech."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whispering","wikidata":"Q1434962"},{"title":"Waterfall","blocks":[{"text":"A waterfall is any point in a river or stream where water flows over a vertical drop or a series of steep drops. Waterfalls also occur where meltwater drops over the edge \nof a tabular iceberg or ice shelf. Waterfalls can be formed in several ways, but the most common method of formation is that a river courses over a top layer of resistant bedrock before falling onto softer rock, which erodes faster, leading to an increasingly high fall. Waterfalls have been studied for their impact on species living in and around them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG/330px-Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG?utm_source=e